  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 229 AM EDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\n- Patchy Dense Fog Possible This Morning\n\nAreas of fog have developed under breaks in the clouds this morning \nas light winds favor enhanced radiational cooling. At times we've \nseen some obs such as Freemont, Charlotte, and Marshall go dense fog \nwith sub 1/4SM visbys. This is likely to continue through shortly \nafter daybreak where we get pockets of clearing. The greatest fog \npotential looks to be areas east of US131, especially near and \nsouth of I96.\n\n- Showers and Thunderstorms Through Tonight\n\nA frontal boundary nearby will lead to periods of showers and \nthunderstorms through tonight, with high PWATs favoring the \npotential for heavy rain. The best chance will come tonight with a \nlow-level jet interacting with the frontal boundary to our south. \nThis will being the best shower and thunderstorm potential along and \nsouth of I96, especially near I94. Drier conditons then take hold \nfor Thursday and Friday as the frontal boundary is shunted south, \nthough isolated showers/storms cannot be ruled out.\n\n- Heavy Rain Possible This Weekend\n\nAttention then turns to this weekend as a mid-level wave slowly \ndrives a low pressure system across the region. Rain starts Friday \nnight continuing into Saturday. The slow nature of this system in \naddition to high (aoa 2\") PWATs supports a heavy rain threat. \nProbabilistic data shows a 70-80% chance of over 1\" of rain across \nmuch of the area with a 40-50% chance of exceeding 2\" mainly across \nthe southern half. This aligns well with the Slight (2/4) Excessive \nRainfall outlook from WPC which we agree with. Marginal instability \nwill support some thunder risk, albeit low given the best \ninstability remains south.\n\nThe forecast becomes more nebulous into early next week as southwest \nflow with embedded shortwaves develops across the area as larger \nscale troughing arrives upstream. Dependent on placement and timing \nof key features, additional showers and thunderstorms are possible.",
